CORE
main.c
--64 --datarace --no-assertions --unwind 5 --rounds 2 --no-por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --graphml-witness /dev/stdout
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
<data key="unroll-bound">3</data>
<data key="architecture">64bit</data>
--
^warning: ignoring
<data key="architecture">32bit</data>
--
Without unroll-bound Dartagnan validated at one unrolling and answered PASS when
the path needed more (per-thread-index-bitmask-race-2). The bound is what the
path needs (two iterations, so 3), not --unwind: goblint tasks run under
--unwind 10001 and Dartagnan was told to unroll 10001 times.
